---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import families from '../../data/families.json';
const rows=families.flatMap(f=>f.inference.map(r=>({...r,name:f.name})));
const statuses=['implemented','historically recoverable','available but missing','unreviewed','invalid for the procedure'];
const repo='https://github.com/JonasMoss/univariateML/blob/master/';
const source=(path)=>repo+path;
---
<Layout title="Inference availability" description="Inference by family, regime and hypothesis, with assumptions and calibration evidence.">
<p class="eyebrow">Methods and their limits · C++ only</p>
<h1>Inference availability</h1>
<p class="summary">Choose a family, a parameter regime and a hypothesis. Availability belongs to that combination, with its nuisance assumptions and evidence.</p>
<div class="notices"><p>These procedures are opt-in <strong>C++ only</strong>. R and JavaScript expose none of them yet. The R parametric percentile bootstrap has not been audited for validity.</p><p>Implemented does not mean well calibrated at every sample size. Read the calibration tables: several Wald intervals under-cover substantially.</p></div>
<details class="guide"><summary>How to read the statuses and regularity</summary>
<dl>
<dt>Implemented</dt><dd>A named C++ procedure exists with derivation and checks. Calibration applies only to the reported sampling grid.</dd>
<dt>Historically recoverable</dt><dd>A procedure can be recovered from verified historical sources. No procedure currently meets this evidence standard: historical derivative names and symbolic grids alone do not qualify.</dd>
<dt>Available but missing</dt><dd>The linked theory or statistic supports a method, but the stated interface or complete inversion is missing. Implementation links identify supporting code, not a finished procedure.</dd>
<dt>Unreviewed</dt><dd>No audited procedure for this scope. This is not proof that inference is impossible. “Other hypotheses” preserves the inventory regime without extrapolating the reviewed targets.</dd>
<dt>Invalid for the procedure</dt><dd>The named method or assumption fails here. A different target or exact method may still work.</dd>
</dl>
<p>Differentiability in quadratic mean (DQM) is a local property of the model. It does not establish estimator consistency or a normal limit. Finite information, its rank, suitability of a pointwise Hessian and estimator asymptotics are separate questions. Known nuisance parameters must be genuinely fixed constants.</p>
<p>Model Fisher information, observed Hessian, sums of observation score cross-products and estimating-equation sensitivity have distinct meanings. An optimizer inverse Hessian or total-score outer product is not a substitute. Robust sandwich claims require their own sampling and moment assumptions.</p>
<p>Exact means finite-sample under the declared assumptions; model-only means no misspecification guarantee. Root-n and rate n describe estimator scaling, not coverage-error rates. Pointwise tests need not produce a connected confidence interval.</p>
<ul><li><a href={source('dev/roadmap/2026-10-30-inference-and-dqm.md')}>Inference roadmap (repository path)</a></li>{[1,4,5].map(i=><li><a href={source(`dev/research/evaluations/2026-10-31-inference-${i}-report.md`)}>TASK-102.{i}: {i===1?'DQM and rank':i===4?'pilot calibration':'exact and nonregular procedures'}</a></li>)}<li><a href={source('dev/validation/inference-availability.json')}>Canonical availability data</a> · <a href={source('dev/validation/inference_availability.py')}>reproducible generator</a></li></ul>
<p>Links name repository paths on master; the current worktree may contain changes not yet published. The acceptance checks validate these paths and evidence anchors locally.</p>
</details>
<div class="filters" id="inference-filters" hidden>
<label>Status<select id="status"><option value="">All statuses</option>{statuses.map(s=><option value={s}>{s}</option>)}</select></label>
<label>Family<select id="family"><option value="">All 98 families</option>{families.map(f=><option value={f.id}>{f.name} · {f.id}</option>)}</select></label>
<label>Regime contains<input id="regime" type="search" placeholder="e.g. endpoint known"/></label>
<button id="reset" type="button">Reset</button>
</div>
<p class="count" id="row-count" aria-live="polite">{rows.length} rows · 98 families · {rows.filter(r=>r.status==='implemented').length} implemented scopes</p>
<noscript><p>All rows and evidence are shown below. Browser search can locate a family; interactive filters require JavaScript.</p></noscript>
<div class="availability"><table><caption>Procedures by family, regime and target</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Family / regime</th><th scope="col">Target and availability</th><th scope="col">Theory, assumptions and evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{rows.map((r,i)=><tr data-inference-row data-status={r.status} data-family={r.family} data-regime={r.regime.toLowerCase()} id={`scope-${i}`}>
<td><a href={`/distributions/${r.family}/`}>{r.name}</a><p class="regime">{r.regime}</p></td>
<td><span class:list={['status',{'implemented':r.status==='implemented','invalid':r.status==='invalid for the procedure'}]}>{r.status}</span><strong>{r.target}</strong><p>{r.procedures}</p></td>
<td><p class="theory">{r.theory}</p><details><summary>Assumptions, evidence and gaps</summary><p>{r.assumptions}</p><p><b>DQM:</b> {r.dqm}<br/><b>Information:</b> {r.information}<br/><b>Rank:</b> {r.rank}</p>
<p><a href={source(r.evidence)}>Derivation / source</a>{r.calibration&&<> · <a href={source(r.calibration)}>Calibration table</a></>}</p>
{r.implementation.map(x=><p><a href={source(x.path)}><code>{x.function}</code></a></p>)}
{r.checks.length>0&&<p>Checks: {r.checks.map(p=><a href={source(p)}>{p.endsWith('.py')?'Calibration driver':'C++ cases'} </a>)}</p>}
{r.gap&&<p><b>Limitation / open:</b> {r.gap}</p>}
{r.historical_sources&&r.historical_sources!=='none_found'&&<p>Historical names: <code>{r.historical_sources}</code>. {r.historical_validation}; not validated for current inference.</p>}
</details></td></tr>)}
</tbody></table></div>
<p id="no-results" hidden>No scopes match these filters. Reset to see all rows.</p>
</Layout>
<style>
.availability table{display:table;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}.availability th:first-child{width:22%}.availability th:nth-child(2){width:33%}.availability td{vertical-align:top;overflow-wrap:anywhere;padding:.9rem .8rem .9rem 0}.availability p{margin:.35rem 0}.availability strong{display:block;line-height:1.4}.regime{font:.75rem/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#59645d}.theory{font-style:italic}.status{display:inline-block;font:.65rem/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;background:#e9e6dd;padding:.15rem .4rem;margin-bottom:.5rem;border-radius:3px}.status.implemented{background:#dce9df;color:#234c35}.status.invalid{background:#f1e0d8;color:#7c352b}.availability summary{font-size:.75rem}.availability details{margin:.4rem 0}.availability caption{text-align:left;margin:.5rem 0;font-size:.8rem}.guide dt{font-weight:bold}.guide dd{margin:0 0 .7rem}#inference-filters[hidden]{display:none}
@media(max-width:650px){.availability table,.availability tbody{display:block}.availability thead{display:none}.availability tr{display:block;border-top:1px solid #aaa99a;padding:.8rem 0}.availability td{display:block;border:0;padding:.25rem 0}.availability tr[hidden]{display:none}.availability td:first-child>a{font-size:1.1rem}.availability caption{display:block}.filters label{width:100%}.filters select,.filters input{width:100%}}
</style>
<script>
const filters=document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#inference-filters')!;
const status=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#status')!,family=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#family')!,regime=document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#regime')!;
const rows=[...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLTableRowElement>('[data-inference-row]')];
function filter(){let count=0;for(const r of rows){r.hidden=!!((status.value&&r.dataset.status!==status.value)||(family.value&&r.dataset.family!==family.value)||!r.dataset.regime!.includes(regime.value.trim().toLowerCase()));if(!r.hidden)count++;}document.querySelector('#row-count')!.textContent=`${count} of ${rows.length} rows`;document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#no-results')!.hidden=count!==0;}
filters.hidden=false;for(const input of [status,family,regime])input.addEventListener('input',filter);
document.querySelector('#reset')!.addEventListener('click',()=>{status.value=family.value=regime.value='';filter();});
</script>
